  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\text{CH} \\iff \\neg\\exists\\kappa : \\text{Cardinal},\\, \\aleph_0 < \\kappa < \\mathfrak{c}",
    "plain": "Starting from the denumerability of ℚ (|ℚ| = ℵ₀), what cardinals lie between |ℚ| and |ℝ|? This is exactly the Continuum Hypothesis, proved independent of ZFC by Gödel and Cohen.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "The denumerability of the rationals is the entry point to the hierarchy of infinite cardinalities.",
      "The continuum hypothesis asks whether any cardinal lies strictly between countable infinity and the continuum.",
      "The Lean entry separates formal cardinal consequences from axiomatized independence facts."
    ]
  },
